{"kind":"finding","id":"F-map-render-025-01","file":"Rendering/AnchorCorrectionTests.cs","line":64,"method":"AnchorSource_AllValuesUnderByte","category":"T1","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Rendering/AnchorCorrection.cs:20; dropping the ': byte' backing type -> still green; only adding a member above 255 -> red","what_it_asserts":"Every AnchorSource and AnchorSide member has an int value in [0,255].","why_weak":"Both enums carry a byte backing type (AnchorCorrection.cs:20 and :42), so the compiler already forbids a member above 255; the widening the test comment names as the risk leaves the assertion green.","proposed_action":"Assert the backing type instead: Enum.GetUnderlyingType(typeof(AnchorSource)) == typeof(byte), which is the fact the .pann byte layout depends on.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-map-render-025-02","file":"Rendering/AnchorCorrectionTests.cs","line":40,"method":"AnchorCorrection_Default_HasZeroEpsilon","category":"T1","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Rendering/AnchorCorrection.cs:62; no edit inside the readonly struct can red this; only changing AnchorCorrection to a class -> red","what_it_asserts":"default(AnchorCorrection) has zero Epsilon, zero UT, null RecordingId and slot-0 enum values.","why_weak":"Those are C# language guarantees for a struct default rather than production decisions, so no realistic change reds the cell; it does not guard the RenderSessionState.TryLookup out-param concern its comment claims.","proposed_action":"Replace with a behavioral cell on the consumer: a missing-key RenderSessionState.TryLookup returns false and the caller applies no translation.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
